I2C Data Frames 
---------------

1. Byte Write Frame 

	This frame is used to write 1 byte data from master to slave 

2. Byte Read Frame 

	This frame is used to read 1 byte data from slave to master 



I2C Byte Write Frame 
--------------------
		
        1 bit 	8 bits    1 bit    8 bits    1 bit   8 bits   1 bit   1 bit
	[ S ] [ SA + W ] [ ACK ] [ Mr Addr ] [ ACK ] [ Data ] [ Ack ] [ P ]

	S -> start condition 

	SA + W -> Slave Addr + option 

	ACK -> 1 bit ack from slave 

	Mr Addr -> Memory address (1 byte) where data write takes place 

	Data -> Data (1 byte) to be written in the given mr address

	P -> stop condition


I2C Byte Read Frame / Random Read Frame
---------------------------------------

	[S] [SA+W] [ACK] [Mr addr] [ACK] [RS] [SA+R] [ACK] [Data Read] [NACK] [P]

	|<---------Dummy write-------->|	

	S :- Start condition 
	
	SA + W :- Slave address + write option 
	
	Mr Addr :- Memory address from which reads takes plaace 

	RS :- Restart condition / start again 
	
	NACK :- No acknowledgement 
	
	P :- Stop condition 

	SA + R :- Slave address + Read option 


