					I2C Slave (SA : 0xB0)

	
	* In I2C protocol default value of I2C bus is '1' when the master and slave is not communicating. 

	* Start Condition :- Will change the idle condition of the I2C bus to signal the i2c slave.

	* After the START condition, the master sends the slave address, and all slaves listen to the bus; only the slave whose address matches will respond.

	* The slave will store the received slave address into temp register and after that it will compare it with its own address. If it is matched the slave will produce ack bit.

		If not present no ack 

	* After ACK master has to send memory address 

	* If this memory address is available in the memory then only the slave will produce the acknowledgment bit

	* After this the master has to send stop condition (I2C Bus becomes idle) 

	* Here we are providing 0x2 as address & if we write a data into it the address counter will automatically increment (like file ptr).

	
